I remember that Nethack once enountered a disk-space problem in one of
my games (while changing levels, the attempt to store the level file
failed) on an old system with very limited harddisk ressources. But I
was able to open another shell (or even escape to shell) to clean up
the hard disk; then a level change had become possible, the game was
still intact. This experience contributed a lot to my view that
Nethack is a piece of software with exceptional robust design in such
issues (which is still rare in other software). Sadly that it hasn't
been so in the OP's case. My condolences.

